Alphabet A={1,2,3}. S0=(2,13,3), S1=(1,2,13). For an arbitrary infinite directive s in {0,1}^N, Definition12 takes the union of factors of P_d(a), P_d=S_{s0}...S_{s(d-1)}, d>=0,a in A. It does not choose one limiting word or impose primitivity. Conjecture1 states p_L(n)<=3n for every n>=1, including conjugates and twins. Unlike nearby theorems, its wording does not impose rational independence. Finite/non-growing letter images and eventually constant directives cannot be removed. Infinitely many S0 allow Gauss grouping G_k=S1^k S0 and double grouping sigma=G_j G_k; eventually-S1 directives need a separate argument rather than an assumed infinite Gauss decomposition. Relabeling and reversal preserve factor counts, so twins/conjugates are one family.

**Universal finite-prefix bridge, proved here as a helper.** Let F_d be all factors of all three P_d(a). Since every letter c occurs in at least one S_i(a), for both i=0 and i=1, P_d(c) is a factor of P_d S_i(a). Thus F_d is contained in F_(d+1). Definition12 gives L=union F_d. For fixed n, these are increasing subsets of the finite set A^n, hence eventually equal L intersect A^n. Consequently any finite prefix with more than 3n distinct n-factors is a genuine source counterexample under EVERY infinite continuation. Conversely a uniform bound for ALL finite products would imply the conjecture, without primitivity or a limiting-word assumption. Our sample does not prove that uniform bound. This also explains why taking factors of just one image, or truncating an image, cannot prove an upper bound.

**Signed graph attack.** For an extendable language, m(v)=|E(v)|-|Eminus(v)|-|Eplus(v)|+1 and the sum over |v|=n is the second complexity difference. Extendability must be justified before using this identity universally; Definition3 by itself requires only factorial closure. Direct finite-factor counting does not require it. With j,k>0, Proposition28 has left maps A=(1,2,2), B=(undefined,2,3), and right maps C=(1,2,2), D=(undefined,2,1). Undefined endpoints are deleted. The printed final filter in Proposition28 repeats the left-map expression; the computations implement the stated two endpoint maps, not that typographical repetition.

